On Thu, 22 Dec 2005, Simon Tatham wrote:

> One puzzle game which would fit reasonably well into a roguelike
> framework is `Inertia',

You seem to interpret "fit reasonably well" technically; can this puzzle
be implemented in NetHack with its limitations on in-/output and its game
mechanics? But the similarity in game /play/ to the rest of the game
should be considered also. Do we want a dungeon crawling game (a
roguelike!) with Sokoban, or do we want tile-based puzzles, connected by a
dungeon crawling game? As nice as puzzle games may be, they should not
have a prominent place in a roguelike game, IMO.

